   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the insurance law, in relation to insurance coverage for drugs used in cancer treatment",
    "basePrintNo": "S7408",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7408-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§3216, 3221, 4303 & 4900, Ins L",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7408\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the insurance law, in relation to insurance coverage\nfor drugs used in cancer treatment\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nTo update the established reference compendia which are used as\nauthoritative sources for use in the determination of off-label drugs\nand biologicals used in an anticancer chemotherapeutic regimen.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSections 3216, 3221, 4303 and 4900 of the Insurance Law are amended to\nupdate the listed standard reference compendia and to allow for future\nupdates to be made without the need for special legislation.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nA uniform policy for the reimbursement of drugs utilized in the\ntreatment of cancer was originally established in New York in 1990.\nIncluded in this policy was a listing of standard reference compendia.\nDue to changes in the pharmaceutical reference industry, two out of\nthe three statutorily-named compendia are no longer published.  In\n2008 the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) revised and\nupdated their list of accepted compendia, removing the two compendia\nwhich were no longer published (the American Medical Association Drug\nEvaluations and the United states Pharmacopoeia-Drug Information) and\nadding three additional compendia (NCCN Drugs and Biologics\nCompendium, Thomson Micromedex DrugDex, and Elsevier Gold Standard's\nClinical Pharmacology).\n\nIt is imperative that the laws of New York keep up with the pace of\ninnovation and clinical discovery to allow beneficiaries timely access\nto the most appropriate treatment options in their battle against\ncancer. These well established reference compendia help physicians in\ntheir ability to access cutting-edge cancer treatments for their\npatients.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect on the first of January next succeeding the\ndate on which it shall have become a law, and shall apply to all\npolicies and contracts issued, renewed, modified, altered or amended\non or after such effective date.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
